<title>USA: Nike hires ad firm Goodby, Silverstein - NYT.</title>
<headline>Nike hires ad firm Goodby, Silverstein - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. footwear and apparel company Nike Inc hired San Franciso-based advertising agency Goodby, Silverstein &amp; Partners, a unit of Omnicom Group Inc, the New York Times said on Monday.</p>
<p>It dismissed smaller agency Leap Partnership, a unit of Leap Group Inc, the paper said.</p>
<p>Goodby would handle Nike's Niketown account and broader duties involving how Nike products were presented and sold by other retailers, the paper said.</p>
<p>New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
